yxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T04:34:36-07:00","id":185446,"title":"","content":"This looks almost identical to the trailer for Castlevania: Lords of Shadow 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1983-einlanzer","name":"Einlanzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1983_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T05:02:42-07:00","id":185448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=180253#post180253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As fascinating as this is, It upsets me seeing great stories being profaned like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd bet my left arm that's exactly what the Romanians said when they heard about the newfangled &quot;Dracula&quot; book which that Bram Stoker fellow wrote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-02-2014, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T05:46:25-07:00","id":185453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=184723#post184723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another completely unnecessary villain origin story movie. I'm betting diamonds against walnuts it won't be half as good as the opening sequence of Coppola's <i>Bram Stoker's Dracula</i>.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Since &quot;villain origin&quot; stories have been popular at least since Macbeth (or, hell, Medea!), I'm guessing they're not going to stop making them anytime soon! Although I admit, in thinking about the trailer, my mind's eye keeps stubbornly copy-pasting Gary Oldman in as Dracula!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having no attachment whatsoever to the original, I might consider seeing this movie except that I know exactly how it's going to end. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the destination, it's the journey!<br /> <br /> I've always liked the original book and movies, but you know, I've *seen* Dracula done (more or less) faithfully several times, so I don't mind seeing the story changed up. I quite enjoyed the recent TV series, which just went entertainingly nuts with it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T05:54:08-07:00","id":185455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Einlanzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=185446#post185446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks almost identical to the trailer for Castlevania: Lords of Shadow 2.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having never seen that myself before, let's take a look:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vUcUz5Vo6iw\" data-code=\"vUcUz5Vo6iw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/vUcUz5Vo6iw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> ...Yeah, there could be some homage there, all right!<br /> <br /> The Dracula Untold does look pretty Abyssal, yes, esp with his motivation being to save his people by taking this power to *rid the world* of his enemies. It's a bit different in that he actively seeks out this power, which isn't how it usually works in Exalted. Hmm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T06:17:18-07:00","id":185466,"title":"","content":"It looks pretty bad compared to Francis Ford Coppula's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T07:35:13-07:00","id":185507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=185453#post185453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since &quot;villain origin&quot; stories have been popular at least since Macbeth (or, hell, Medea!), I'm guessing they're not going to stop making them anytime soon!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's an important difference between &quot;here's an original story seen mostly from the perspective of the villain&quot; and &quot;here's a derivative story where we take the villain of that movie/book/whatever and give you two hours of his backstory with no bearing on the events of the original story&quot;. But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T09:15:41-07:00","id":185588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=180253#post180253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As fascinating as this is, It upsets me seeing great stories being profaned like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Universal has been desecrating romanticist monsters for a long time we should all be used to this by now ; D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T09:57:25-07:00","id":185610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this film (even if it's bad) put a final stop to vampire pussyfication and start a new darker vampire trend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark vampires are not automatically better than sparklepusses. Have we learned nothing from Underworld? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T10:11:01-07:00","id":185616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=185610#post185610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark vampires are not automatically better than sparklepusses. Have we learned nothing from Underworld? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But the sparklie ones automatically suck, while dark vampires only may suck. Thus dark vampires are automatically better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T18:47:17-07:00","id":185929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=185616#post185616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the sparklie ones automatically suck, while dark vampires only may suck. Thus dark vampires are automatically better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not just dark vampires:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/3/36657/1317378-count.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Of course, I'd also like to see:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://horde.me/uploads/images/51/5d5d/515d5d58497a2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T05:29:15-07:00","id":186203,"title":"","content":"Imagine if everything you knew about Vampire the Masquerade was the first person account of a lovestruck ghoul with no grasp of vampire politics and just an unwavering devotion that her beautiful vampire prince could do no wrong. That's basically the Twilight Saga.<br /> <br /> Twilight vampires get a lot of flak for being &quot;sparkly&quot; but they're as worthy of their vampire status as any of their predecessors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T05:48:12-07:00","id":186211,"title":"","content":"Eh, it really rubs me the wrong way when current vampire fiction increasingly removes the traditional weaknesses of the vampire for purposes of &quot;romance&quot; or just because it's convenient. And yes, I know the weakness to sunlight is a hollywood invention, but it's been so common, that it's as traditional as any other, now. <br /> <br /> At least the Vampire Diaries actually has a *reason* why some of its vamps are seemingly immune to daylight! <br /> <br /> The worst offender (and logical extension of this) is probably a Korean manwha that people were talking about a while ago, whose bishie vampires not only had NONE of the traditional weaknesses, but they didn't even drink blood! Sooo...WHY are we even calling them vampires, then?!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T06:34:35-07:00","id":186245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=186211#post186211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst offender (and logical extension of this) is probably a Korean manwha that people were talking about a while ago, whose bishie vampires not only had NONE of the traditional weaknesses, but they didn't even drink blood! Sooo...WHY are we even calling them vampires, then?!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Noblesse.<br /> <br /> That was an in-world translation error early on. They just call themselves &quot;Nobles&quot; and are basically just a magically powerful super-human race. If they do drink blood (some do because they enjoy it) then the victims get infected and turned into what we could call vampires (pale, undead creatures who can't stay in the sun). As a result among Nobles it's forbidden to drink human blood, though, you know, the evil Nobles ignore those rules and go do their own thing. So Nobles aren't vampires, but they can make vampires (though this has only been peripherally important in the series so far).<br /> <br /> People in the world often call Nobles vampires because they don't understand the differences, and it actually annoys most Nobles quite a bit when people call them that as they view it as rather insulting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-02-2014, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T08:46:45-07:00","id":186312,"title":"","content":"Ahhh magnificent: I once bring up the diversity of application for the term &quot;vampire&quot; in fiction and folklore in order to illustrate a point about how basically anything could be Exalted, and here we are coming full circle with a thread containing people quibbling over the specificity of what the term &quot;vampire&quot; means. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T09:17:14-07:00","id":186321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=186211#post186211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. And yes, I know the weakness to sunlight is a hollywood invention</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the traditional vampire is nocturnal and spends the day sleeping in a coffin, the only thing Hollywood introduced was them spontaneously combusting if they decided to go out during the day. In the case of Dracula many of his powers stopped working during the day and he needed to rest in the earth of his homeland to recuperate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T09:42:48-07:00","id":186349,"title":"","content":"<i>Nosferatu\u200b </i>was a German production, yo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T09:58:33-07:00","id":186359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=186321#post186321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the traditional vampire is nocturnal and spends the day sleeping in a coffin, the only thing Hollywood introduced was them spontaneously combusting if they decided to go out during the day. In the case of Dracula many of his powers stopped working during the day and he needed to rest in the earth of his homeland to recuperate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in the original Dracula, the &quot;rest in the earth of his homeland&quot; was an amazing twist.<br /> <br /> I mean, until then, vampire myths were all about vampires being tied down to the place of their death, which was a clear weakness and prevented vampires from going places.<br /> <br /> But then here comes Dracula, who has the amazing idea to <i>put Transylvanian dirt in crates so he can sleep in the &quot;earth of his homeland&quot; anywhere. </i>Stroke of genius, which allows him to move from Bumfuck Nowhere, Transylvania to freaking London - the beating heart of civilization, to the mind of the author and his readers.<br /> <br /> ...but then this novel becomes the seminal vampire works, the tenets of vampire myths that existed before are mostly forgotten, and Dracula is treated as the &quot;source material&quot; of vampire stories. Then everyone and their mother does the &quot;carrying earth with you&quot; trick when it is one of their weaknesses at all, which it rarely is, and Dracula appears weird and clunky for needing to carry dirt around. What was once an amazing innovation from the most cunning monster is now seen as a big, cumbersome flaw.<br /> <br /> It's weird how these things happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 07-02-2014, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T18:55:27-07:00","id":186746,"title":"","content":"It bothers me that the Turks are being specifically cast as 'evil' for the purposes of this movie, but other than that could be a fun action film. <br /> <br /> It's clearly not meant to be a traditional 'vampire' film.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1165-hecaton","name":"Hecaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T19:15:18-07:00","id":186757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hecaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=186746#post186746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It bothers me that the Turks are being specifically cast as 'evil' for the purposes of this movie, but other than that could be a fun action film.<br /> <br /> It's clearly not meant to be a traditional 'vampire' film.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this seems to be going for the normal idea that Vlad III (nickname, &quot;the Impaler&quot;) is the vampire Dracula, then the Ottoman empire is the obvious villain for the piece. Hell, it's not even far-fetched: the Ottomans were one of the big groups that were expanding into other areas/conquering them at the time, and they did run up against the historical Vlad III. That generally makes you the bad guys, at least from a modern perspective. Even if an Empire does provide infastructure and the like, it only does so after stomping the subject nation's face into the ground (unless they capitulated before the armies arrived I guess).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T19:25:14-07:00","id":186762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hecaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=186746#post186746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It bothers me that the Turks are being specifically cast as 'evil' for the purposes of this movie, but other than that could be a fun action film.<br /> <br /> It's clearly not meant to be a traditional 'vampire' film.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Vlad III Tepes did actually wage war against an invading Ottoman army. That part is true to history, in the very broadest strokes if not in any of the details.<br /> <br /> What bothers <i>me</i> is that they cast a bunch of white dudes as the Turks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T19:35:25-07:00","id":186769,"title":"","content":"I'm eminently aware that Vlad III fought against the Turks, and my point was not that they are the antagonists, but rather that they are specifically called out as 'evil' in the trailer, when the protagonist is someone who is literally legendary for his cruelty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1165-hecaton","name":"Hecaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T20:22:03-07:00","id":186785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hecaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=186769#post186769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm eminently aware that Vlad III fought against the Turks, and my point was not that they are the antagonists, but rather that they are specifically called out as 'evil' in the trailer, when the protagonist is someone who is literally legendary for his cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was more ruthless than cruel, from what I understand. He went to any length to protect his lands and his people, even if that meant inflicting horrible deaths on prisoners as a warning to his enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T06:46:26-07:00","id":187007,"title":"","content":"Kingdom of Heaven is set during the Crusades, and yet the Muslims in general and Saladin in particular are portrayed as people of depth and nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T08:39:47-07:00","id":187118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=186785#post186785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> He was more ruthless than cruel, from what I understand. He went to any length to protect his lands and his people, even if that meant inflicting horrible deaths on prisoners as a warning to his enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>When a I made a Vlad III Tepes Abyssal for a 2e game, Conviction was his primary Virtue.<br /> <br /> Of course, he also had Dark Messiah Style, which the real Dracula likely didn't have more than one or two Charms of. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T08:41:33-07:00","id":187120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hecaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=186769#post186769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm eminently aware that Vlad III fought against the Turks, and my point was not that they are the antagonists, but rather that they are specifically called out as 'evil' in the trailer, when the protagonist is someone who is literally legendary for his cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that most stories of Vlad's cruelty were fabricated and spread by Germany, who hated his guts for reasons I'm not well able to explain. He sure was a harsh man, but far from the man-eater most people immediately picture. Modern Romanians often view him quite favorably.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that the Ottoman Empire of Dracula's times was a ridiculously cruel tyranny that regularly did unspeakable things to Christians in the lands they conquered. Quite easy to construe them as evil, even if it does paint a very simplified picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T19:11:56-07:00","id":187573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=187007#post187007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kingdom of Heaven is set during the Crusades, and yet the Muslims in general and Saladin in particular are portrayed as people of depth and nuance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's in part because the Crusades were happening in the Muslim territories(and the crusaders got a significant PR boost from what I remember). It's like how if you set a story in, say, the Realm's heartland, you're going to get a much more positive view of the Realm, as opposed to when you show the satraps. Or if you showed Belgium during WW1/2, vs the Belgium Congo under Leopold II's control. The issue here is largely that the Crusaders have much better PR than they deserve.<br /> <br /> Well, that and apparently they can't find Turkish(or Mediterranean) people to play the parts of the Ottomans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T23:10:51-07:00","id":187746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=185507#post185507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's an important difference between &quot;here's an original story seen mostly from the perspective of the villain&quot; and &quot;here's a derivative story where we take the villain of that movie/book/whatever and give you two hours of his backstory with no bearing on the events of the original story&quot;. But that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know that the famous ancient play Medea was an *adaptation* of a myth already old by then, right? And that MacBeth was an actual king whose true life story almost certainly did NOT involve witches, ghosts and goddesses? <br /> <br /> Some of the original audiences of those plays may well have had the same reactions you're having now, is all I'm saying...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T23:21:12-07:00","id":187750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hecaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=186746#post186746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It bothers me that the Turks are being specifically cast as 'evil' for the purposes of this movie, but other than that could be a fun action film.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really seeing that. I mean, granted, the *trailer* says something about &quot;to fight against evil&quot;, yes, but we don't see the Turks doing anything especially evil besides marching to war (which is enough to make them seem such to those they are invading). It looks like Vlad's son is narrating at least some of the story, which may make this something like 300, where the propaganda is actually part of the in-setting story (something many critics seemed to sadly miss). At least it doesn't look like Anastacia, where the Russian Revolution is shown to be literally led by demons!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of course, we won't know for sure until we see it, which I definitely plan to. But I wonder how it will play in Romania, where Vlad is still thought well of? I remember seeing some Romanians on TV, saying that they didn't understand the constant vilification of their hero, and how he was like our George Washington, to them. I wonder how Americans would feel if Europeans just kept making films where Washington was a demonic monster?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T03:35:19-07:00","id":190086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/179892-the-new-dracula-untold-movie-looks-pretty-darn-abyssal?p=187120#post187120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Modern Romanians often view him quite favorably.</div> </div> </div> </div>A culture viewing their folk heroes favourably does not really serve as an effective moral judgement of them. Genghis Khan is viewed favourably by people throughout Mongolia, China, and possibly a couple other places I don't recall, and there's pretty much no doubt that he was responsible for more deaths than Stalin.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}